<title>ITALY: Italy's SACE expects to slash losses in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italy's SACE expects to slash losses in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's export credit guarantee body SACE said it expects to cut its 1996 losses to some 1.6 trillion lire from the 2.63 trillion lire loss registered in 1995.</p>
<p>SACE said in a statement that the effects of a radical restructuring were beginning to be seen and it aimed to be &quot;more rigorous in choosing operations to back and in paying indemnities&quot; as well as pursuing &quot;aggressive action to recover credits from defaulting countries.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
